# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# ---- what was here before, and why it broke the site ----
#
# This file used to rewrite /champions -> /champions.html, and the same for
# items, runes, spells and write, to get extensionless URLs.
#
# Cloudflare Pages already does that. It serves /champions for
# champions.html AND 301-redirects /champions.html -> /champions on its own.
# So the rules made a loop: a link to champions.html got redirected to
# /champions by Cloudflare, rewritten back to /champions.html by this file,
# redirected again, forever. Every nav tab was dead.
#
# The lesson is the boring one: I wrote rules for a platform behaviour I
# had not checked. Pages needs no help here — the pretty URLs work with
# this file empty.

# The masteries page was folded into the guide creator. This one IS a real
# redirect — a different page, not a different spelling of the same one —
# so it cannot loop. masteries.html also carries a meta refresh, which
# covers anyone who has it bookmarked and arrives before this rule applies.
/masteries      /create      301
/masteries.html /create      301
